      "dom_id": "step-q216590",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Negate the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ For all $m\\in N,$ $3m+1$ is not odd.",
      "worked_solution": "If we denote\n\n$$\nP(m):3m+1\\text{ is odd},\n$$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀m\\in N,\\,¬P(m).\n$$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∀m\\in N,\\,¬P(m)) & ≡∃m\\in N,\\,¬¬P(m) \\\\  & ≡∃m\\in N,\\,P(m).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $∃m\\in N,\\,P(m)$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $m\\in N$ such that $3m+1$ is odd.",
